<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/roof-damage.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/roof-damage-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/roof-damage.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/insurance-appraisal-services/">Services</a></li><li aria-current="page">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Roof and Hail Damage Appraisal Across Washington</h1><p class="lede">East of the Cascades, summer thunderstorms can drop damaging hail. West of the mountains, wind and moss do the work. Either way, roof disputes come down to measurements and repairability.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-y" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Common gap</dt><dd>Repair vs. replace</dd></div><div><dt>Key evidence</dt><dd>Test squares &amp; photos</dd></div><div><dt>Roof types</dt><dd>Shingle, metal, low-slope</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>Hail in an inland climate</h2>
<p>Washington doesn’t have the hail reputation of the Great Plains, but the Columbia Basin, the Palouse and the Spokane area see strong summer thunderstorms. Hail that dents gutters and bruises shingles in Spokane Valley or Moses Lake can shorten a roof’s life even when it looks fine from the ground.</p>
<p>West of the Cascades, hail is less frequent and usually smaller. Roof claims there tend to follow windstorms, falling limbs and long wet winters that expose old damage. Insurers sometimes argue that what they see is wear, moss or granule loss from age. Good documentation separates storm damage from maintenance issues.</p>
<h2>The roof disputes we see most</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Slope counts.</strong> The carrier approves two slopes; the damage pattern supports four or the whole roof.</li>
<li><strong>Repairability.</strong> Discontinued shingles, brittle materials or exposure patterns that make spot repair unworkable.</li>
<li><strong>Steep and high charges.</strong> Pitches at 7/12 and up, and two-story eaves, usually add labor and safety costs.</li>
<li><strong>Underlayment, flashing and ventilation.</strong> Items required by code or manufacturer instructions when a roof is replaced.</li>
<li><strong>Metal roofing and soft metals.</strong> Cosmetic-damage exclusions and how they apply to panels, vents and gutters.</li>
</ul>
<h2>How we document a roof</h2>
<p>We measure every slope, record pitch, count layers and photograph damage with scale references. Where helpful, we lay out test squares the way adjusters and engineers do so the panel sees comparable evidence. Then we price tear-off, disposal, materials and labor for your county.</p>
<p>Use our <a href="/free-claim-calculators/roof-pitch-squares-calculator/">roof pitch and squares calculator</a> to compare your roof’s size against the carrier’s estimate before you call.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>The insurer says my roof damage is wear and tear. Can appraisal help?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>If the insurer denies that a covered loss happened at all, that’s a coverage question appraisal may not resolve. If it accepts storm damage but disputes how much, appraisal is often a good fit.</p></div></details><details><summary>What is a cosmetic damage exclusion?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Some policies exclude dents to metal roofing or other surfaces that don’t affect function. Whether a particular dent is cosmetic is often argued on the facts, and the wording matters.</p></div></details><details><summary>How old can hail damage be?<svg class="ico chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>There’s no single cut-off, but late reporting gives the insurer room to question when damage occurred. Report promptly and keep weather records for the date of loss.</p></div></details></div><h2>Related services</h2><div class="cards3 tight"><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/storm-sky.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/storm-sky-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/storm-sky.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Appraisal</h3><span class="pcard-p">Pacific windstorms, bomb cyclones and the occasional tornado: torn roofs, siding, fences and outbuildings.</span><span class="pcard-more">Learn more <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/tree-impact-claim-appraisal/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/fallen-tree-house.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/fallen-tree-house-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/fallen-tree-house.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Fallen Tree Damage Appraisal</h3><span class="pcard-p">Douglas fir, cedar and maple impacts on roofs, framing and decks, plus removal and crane costs.</span><span class="pcard-more">Learn more <svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a><a class="pcard rv" href="/insurance-appraisal-services/water-rain-intrusion-appraisal/"><span class="pcard-img"><img src="/assets/img/photos/water-damage.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/water-damage-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/water-damage.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="pcard-body"><span class="pcard-k">Related service</span><h3 class="pcard-t">Water &amp; Rain Intrusion Appraisal</h3><span 